{
 "title": "High-Dimensional Probability",
 "byline": "Roman Vershynin \u00b7 Cambridge University Press, 2018 (author\u2019s version)",
 "note": "End-of-chapter notes are not broken out. Summaries are in our own words; the text stays in the PDF.",
 "summary": "An introduction to probability in high dimensions aimed at data science. Vershynin builds the toolkit of concentration inequalities (Hoeffding, Chernoff, Bernstein, sub-gaussian and sub-exponential variables), extends it to random vectors and random matrices via nets and covering numbers, and then to dependence (Lipschitz concentration, matrix Bernstein, Hanson\u2013Wright, symmetrization). The second half covers random processes and chaining (Slepian, Sudakov, Dudley, generic chaining, VC dimension), matrix deviation inequalities and their geometry, sparse recovery and the lasso, and Dvoretzky\u2013Milman. Every tool is paired with an application: community detection, covariance estimation, Grothendieck\u2019s inequality and max-cut, Johnson\u2013Lindenstrauss, matrix completion and learning theory.",
